# Line endings are part of the data here, not a matter of taste.
#
# The Windows runner checks out with core.autocrlf=true, which turns every LF into CRLF.
# For the VT fixtures that changes the byte stream they decode to -- a stray CR moves the
# cursor to column 0 -- and for the baselines it changes the bytes they are compared
# against. Both would show up as a difference that no code change could explain.
#
# eol=lf is therefore not a style choice: it is what makes the comparison mean the same
# thing on all three runners.
* text=auto eol=lf
tests/fixtures/** text eol=lf
tests/baselines/** text eol=lf
